# Security audit

Several security decisions are good:

**Authentication:** credentials are hashed; unknown-email verification uses a dummy hash to reduce enumeration timing differences.

**Authorization:** `/admin` is protected by middleware/proxy and independently server-checked.

**Registration:** new users always receive `USER`; admin promotion is out-of-band.

**Rate limiting:** raw email/IP identifiers are HMACed before storage.

**Affiliate redirects:** destination is server-controlled and HTTPS-only.

**CMS:** article HTML uses a strict allowlist and is sanitised on write and again before rendering.

**External article links:** receive `noopener noreferrer`.

**Embeds:** arbitrary iframes are not accepted; only typed YouTube/Vimeo markers are rendered.

**Security headers:** HSTS, nosniff, frame restrictions, Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy are configured.

The remaining major issue is operational:

```text
CSP is report-only until verified
edge/WAF rate limiting not yet confirmed
```

Do not set the confirmation flags until actual production verification occurs.

